<title>GREECE: GREEK CLOSED-END FUND PERFORMANCE IN MAY.</title>
<headline>GREEK CLOSED-END FUND PERFORMANCE IN MAY.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's 16 closed-end investment</p>
<p>funds listed on the Athens bourse had a market capitalisation of</p>
<p>183.2 billion drachmas at the end of May, up 28.5 percent from</p>
<p>142.7 billion in April, the Association of Institutional</p>
<p>Investors said.</p>
<p>Statistics showed that 10 out of the 16 funds were trading</p>
<p>at a discount to their net asset value (NAV) at the end of May.</p>
<p>Total NAV amounted to 170.7 billion drachmas versus 150.3</p>
<p>billion at the end of April.</p>
<p>Closed-end funds traded at an average premium of 7.4 percent</p>
<p>to market capitalisation. They had traded at an average 5.1</p>
<p>percent discount a month earlier.</p>
<p>The funds raised their equity allocation in May to 76.5</p>
<p>percent from 75.2 percent in April.</p>
<p>    ASSET CLASS	   May 30 1997	  April 30 1997</p>
<p>    Equity		    76.5%		    75.2%</p>
<p>     - Greek		  68.6%		    66.3%</p>
<p>     - Foreign		 7.9%		     8.9%</p>
<p>    Fixed income	    14.8%		    16.3%</p>
<p>    Cash			 8.4%		     8.8%</p>
<p>Only five funds managed to outperform the market's 71.3</p>
<p>percent climb in the first five months of this year.</p>
<p>    FUND	 MKT CAP*	 SHARE**   PREMIUM/</p>
<p>		   (drs bln)	RETURN    DISCOUNT</p>
